WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Module review · People, Culture & Volunteers
Recap: People, Culture & Volunteers

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Bring your people decisions into one plan you can use as your first people join.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
You planned the people your work needs and how you will treat them: fair recruitment, clear terms, a good start, regular check-ins, fair pay, a healthy culture, valued volunteers and planned exits.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
One lesson at a time

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:36.289
4.1 Workforce planning: Workforce planning matches time and skills to the work over time, including what founders carry themselves.

6
00:00:36.289 --> 00:00:46.407
4.2 Recruitment and fair selection: Your first role sets the standard: plain adverts and only the criteria the work needs keep selection fair.

7
00:00:46.407 --> 00:00:56.044
4.3 Contracts and terms: Every working relationship needs written terms that suit its type, including the one between co-founders.

8
00:00:56.444 --> 00:00:57.044
One lesson at a time

9
00:00:57.044 --> 00:01:06.052
4.4 Onboarding: Good onboarding covers mission, role, safeguards and ways of working, and your first people shape it for everyone.

10
00:01:06.052 --> 00:01:15.059
4.5 Check-ins, performance and development: Short, regular check-ins, starting now between co-founders, do more for performance than an annual appraisal.

11
00:01:15.059 --> 00:01:25.067
4.6 Pay, careers and recognition: Pay shows your values, and principles set before the first salary prevent unfair gaps later.

12
00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:26.067
One lesson at a time

13
00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:36.185
4.7 Culture, wellbeing and inclusion: Culture forms in the first months, mostly from what founders do, and either supports or contradicts your values.

14
00:01:36.185 --> 00:01:45.933
4.8 Volunteers and community contributors: Volunteering works as a two-way relationship, clear about what you offer as well as what you ask.

15
00:01:45.933 --> 00:01:56.311
4.9 Offboarding, handover and continuity: Everyone leaves one day, including you; a planned exit protects both the organisation and the person.

16
00:01:56.911 --> 00:02:09.881
Next you choose the minimum internal systems to run it all, with people systems as one part of a map that also covers finance, compliance, information and tools.

17
00:02:10.481 --> 00:02:15.281
You check your People Plan and download each exercise as a PDF.

18
00:02:16.781 --> 00:02:19.881
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
